# The Narrative Arc: from one tool to a shipping swarm

Run this top to bottom. Each act proves one claim; the finale uses all of them.
Timings assume a warm `_build` (`mix test` once first).

## Act 1 — One tool, supervised (5 min)

Claim: a tool can die any death and the session never notices.

```sh
mix demo.crash
mix showcase budgets
mix showcase calc
```

Watch for: `{:error, ...}` where Python would raise; the harness continuing
on the next line. Then `notebooks/tool_crash.livemd` for the interactive
version. Primitives: `Task.Supervisor`, `Task.yield`, AST whitelisting.

## Act 2 — Memory that outlives processes (5 min)

Claim: OTP ships the database.

```sh
mix showcase memory
mix demo.memory
```

Watch for: ETS gone with its owner (`:undefined`), Mnesia rows surviving,
one file snapshot restoring a murdered session. Then
`notebooks/memory.livemd`. Primitives: `:ets`, `:mnesia`, `:dets`.

## Act 3 — Many agents (5 min)

Claim: orchestration without a queue, a registry lib, or a pubsub dep.

```sh
mix showcase registry
mix showcase pg
mix showcase backpressure
mix showcase plan
```

Watch for: named calls with no pid plumbing, observations arriving via
`:pg` + `send`, 8×200ms in ~800ms at `max_concurrency: 2`, a diamond plan
halting only the failed branch. Then `notebooks/parallel.livemd`.
Primitives: `DynamicSupervisor`, `Registry`, `:pg`, `async_stream`, macros.

## Act 4 — Many nodes (5 min)

Claim: same code, two machines, one kill -9.

```sh
mix showcase cluster
```

Watch for: 6/6 across nodes, `:nodedown` arriving unprompted, 3/6 + 3
`badrpc` — batch completes anyway. Tests do the same in 0.3s with `:peer`.
Then `notebooks/cluster.livemd`. Primitives: distribution, `Node.monitor`,
`:rpc`, `:peer`.

## Act 5 — See everything (5 min)

Claim: the VM already knows; we just render it.

```sh
mix showcase trace
mix dashboard  # http://localhost:4000, then mix showcase telemetry
```

Watch for: a full call path with zero instrumentation, a supervision tree
that is `which_children` all the way down, tool timings arriving over
PubSub. Then `notebooks/tracing.livemd`. Primitives: `:dbg`,
`:telemetry`, LiveView.

## Act 6 — Survive everything (5 min)

Claim: fault tolerance as flags, and upgrades without restarts.

```sh
mix showcase chaos
mix showcase restarts
mix showcase upgrade
mix demo.toon_stats
```

Watch for: same-name recovery, `:temporary` vanishing by design,
`rest_for_one` ordering, v1 greeting then v2 in one VM, and the honest
token numbers (TOON ≈ −50% uniform, +40% nested — selective, not dogma).

## Finale — The overnight release train (5 min)

Everything above, one story: a role swarm ships rate limiting to a
fixture service while a worker dies, a node dies, and the scoring policy
upgrades mid-run.

```sh
mix poc.release_train --clean   # the control group
mix poc.release_train           # chaos armed: still ships
```

Then `notebooks/release_train.livemd`. Open `mix dashboard` alongside and
watch the train arrive live.
